{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-294685-r4587421","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Yogurt Cupcakes (Vegan)","sourcePageId":294685,"sourceRevision":"4587421","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-26T23:35:58Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Codename Noreste","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Yogurt%20Cupcakes%20(Vegan)&oldid=4587421","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:29:26.986Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes for muffins","Category:Recipes using applesauce","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using canola oil","Category:Recipes using cornstarch","Category:Recipes using dark chocolate","Category:Recipes using marzipan","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes using white sugar","Category:Recipes using yogurt","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Vegan recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"82902999f141b55a40f46535ebf175a605c47f9c4506154a7565906ea032cda8","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary\n| category = Recipes for dessert\n| time = 30–45 minutes\n| difficulty = 2\n}}\n{{recipe}}\n==Ingredients==\n=== Cupcakes ===\n\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (118 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) vanilla soy [[Cookbook:Yogurt|yogurt]] \n* ⅔ cup (158 ml) vanilla or plain [[Cookbook:Soy Milk|soy milk]] \n* ¼ cup (60 ml) [[Cookbook:Applesauce|applesauce]] \n* ¾ cup (177 ml) white [[Cookbook:Granulated Sugar|granulated sugar]]\n* 1 ¼ cup (284 ml) [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]] \n* 3 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Canola Oil|canola oil]]\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Cornstarch|cornstarch]]\n* ¾ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* ¼ teaspoon salt\n* 1 ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Vanilla Extract|vanilla extract]]\n\n=== Topping ===\n* 1 part Soy Cuisine-brand [[Cookbook:Nondairy Milk|cream substitute]]\n* 2–3 parts dark [[Cookbook:Chocolate|chocolate]]\n* Sliced [[Cookbook:Nuts and Seeds|nuts]]\n\n=== Filling ===\n* [[Cookbook:Marzipan|Marzipan]]\n* [[Cookbook:Nougat|Nougat]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 350°F (175°C) and fill muffin pan with [[Cookbook:Cupcake Liner|liners]].\n#Combine liquid and dry ingredients separately, then whisk together the liquid and dry mixtures.\n#Fill the liners ~75% full, and let them [[Cookbook:Baking|bake]] for 22–24 minutes.\n#Let them cool completely, then unmold them.\n#Meanwhile, melt the chocolate and soy cuisine together for topping. This mixture should be smooth. Cool slightly.\n# Carve a little cone out of the center of each muffin. Fill the cavity with fruit or nougat or marzipan to give your cupcake a little heart. Replace the cutout cone on top.\n# Top the muffins with the chocolate topping and some sliced nuts.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* You can substitute strawberry soy yogurt for the vanilla soy yogurt.\n* Silicone [[Cookbook:Cupcake Liner|cupcake liners]] work better than paper ones. \n\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using yogurt]]\n[[Category:Recipes for muffins]]\n[[Category:Recipes using marzipan]]\n[[Category:Recipes using applesauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dark chocolate]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornstarch]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using canola oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Yogurt Cupcakes (Vegan)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ cup (118 ml) vanilla soy yogurt","sourceText":"½ cup (118 ml) vanilla soy yogurt","amountText":"½ cup (118 ml) vanilla soy yogurt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"⅔ cup (158 ml) vanilla or plain soy milk","sourceText":"⅔ cup (158 ml) vanilla or plain soy milk","amountText":"⅔ cup (158 ml) vanilla or plain soy milk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"¼ cup (60 ml) applesauce","sourceText":"¼ cup (60 ml) applesauce","amountText":"¼ cup (60 ml) applesauce","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"¾ cup (177 ml) white granulated sugar","sourceText":"¾ cup (177 ml) white granulated sugar","amountText":"¾ cup (177 ml) white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 ¼ cup (284 ml) flour","sourceText":"1 ¼ cup (284 ml) flour","amountText":"1 ¼ cup (284 ml) flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"3 tablespoons canola oil","sourceText":"3 tablespoons canola oil","amountText":"3 tablespoons canola oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"2 tablespoons cornstarch","sourceText":"2 tablespoons cornstarch","amountText":"2 tablespoons cornstarch","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"¾ teaspoon baking powder","sourceText":"¾ teaspoon baking powder","amountText":"¾ teaspoon baking pow